# Feature Specification: Subscription-Filtered Screen News over WebSocket

**Feature Branch**: N/A (spec authored in place; no branch created)  
**Created**: 2026-10-03  
**Status**: Draft, user-approved scope (2026-10-03)  
**Identity/persistence clarification**: User-directed (2026-10-04): required new authenticated `mbook-quarkus` persistence endpoint; WebSocket client ID is the existing iOS deviceid; server-side simple-web-api active-session lookup (integration not implemented).  
**Identity trust-model correction**: User-directed (2026-10-04): the active-session list holds authenticated users, so fresh unique list membership of the supplied deviceid is sufficient WebSocket identity; no separate WebSocket caller-session binding is required (see "Accepted WebSocket identity trust model").  
**Storage decision**: User-directed correction (2026-10-03): shared `login_.news_settings`, literal lowercase `yes`/`no`; row presence is not eligibility.  
**Owner constraints**: USER-APPROVED REQUIRED target (2026-10-03): `news_settings.logins_id NOT NULL` + `UNIQUE (logins_id)`; not deployed.  
**Architecture**: [`speckit.system.screen-news-websocket-subscriptions.architecture.md`](./speckit.system.screen-news-websocket-subscriptions.architecture.md)  
**Database schema**: [Current baseline, approved owner constraints and pending hardening](./speckit.system.screen-news-websocket-subscriptions.database-schema.md)  
**Plan / Tasks**: [`speckit.system.screen-news-websocket-subscriptions.plan`](./speckit.system.screen-news-websocket-subscriptions.plan), [`speckit.system.screen-news-websocket-subscriptions.tasks`](./speckit.system.screen-news-websocket-subscriptions.tasks)  
**Input**: User description: "add feature specify about websocket server receiving client ids on connection and the server will just send message if the user is subscribed to receiving news on screen add, update or delete."
**User storage correction**: "news_settings table will hold if the user is subscribed to certain kind of news, now newsScreening. so the columns may grow, but it shall contain yes, or put to no, once unsubscribed"
**User owner-constraint confirmation**: "yes, i omitted the direct answer, but yes: Enforce one row per user with a NOT NULL plus UNIQUE change"
**User identity correction (2026-10-04)**: "correct: GET /simple-service-webapp/webapi/myresource/admin holds users, that are authenticated, so membership is enough."

## Domain terminology (repository evidence)

- **Screen** = a scheduled screening record (movie + venue + date/time + screen id + screening-date id), not a UI screen.
  Evidence: `mbooks-quarkus` admin operations `/book/admin/addscreen`, `/book/admin/updatescreen`,
  `/book/admin/deletescreen` in `VenueController`; `DAO.insertNewScreen/updateScreen/deleteScreen`;
  iOS admin flows `AdminVC` / `AdminUpdateVC`.
- **Screen news** = the notification produced when a screen changes. Today only *add* publishes one
  (`publishAddedMovie` → `AddMovie {movie, date, venue, screeningId, screeningDatesId}` → topic
  `ios-movies-notifications2`). Update and delete publish nothing.
- **News subscription** = a per-user news preference. Evidence: `mbook-quarkus` entity `NewsSettings`
  (`news_settings.newsScreening`, linked to `logins`). No code currently reads or writes it.
  **Decided by user (2026-10-03)**: `news_settings` is shared per-user news preferences, currently
  `newsScreening`, with future columns for other news categories. Exact lowercase text
  `newsScreening='yes'` = subscribed; `newsScreening='no'` = unsubscribed. Row existence is
  **not** eligibility. Subscribe ensures a settings row and sets only this column to `yes`;
  unsubscribe sets only this column to `no`, retaining the row and all unrelated preferences.
  Missing row defaults off; new managed rows start at `no` unless explicitly subscribing.
  Existing NULL/unknown values never imply opt-in; validation errors must be explicit.
  `login_.news_settings` is present in the designated schema snapshot
  `k8infra/mysql_8/Dump20260524.sql:372–379`, but its user FK is nullable and non-unique and it has
  a nullable `VARCHAR(255)` preference. `logins_id NOT NULL` + `UNIQUE (logins_id)` are
  **USER-APPROVED REQUIRED target constraints**, not deployed: at most one row per account,
  every settings row has an owner. They do not create rows for every user; no blanket backfill.
  Preference-column NOT NULL/default/CHECK remain pending approval. Shared-row storage is decided,
  not an open dedicated-table-versus-reuse choice.
- **WebSocket server** = `@ServerEndpoint("/ws")` in `mbook-quarkus` (exposed as `/mbook-1/ws`, used by iOS
  `URLManager.webSocketURL`) and an identical endpoint in `mbooks-quarkus` (`/mbooks-1/ws`). Both currently
  **broadcast every screen-add message to every connected session**, without identifying the client or checking a subscription.
- **iOS menu screen** = `MenuVC` (`SwiftCinemas/SwiftLoginScreen/MenuVC.swift`), a UIKit screen with the profile card,
  `Admin` button, `Back`/`Purchases` navigation, and logout. It has no news control today.
- **Client ID** = the existing iOS **deviceid**, sent on connect and reconnect, not a newly
  generated app identifier. Repository spelling is `deviceId`: `currentDeviceId()` in
  `SwiftCinemas/SwiftLoginScreen/ciphertext.swift:11–14` returns
  `UIDevice.current.identifierForVendor?.uuidString ?? ""`; `LoginVC.swift:94–101` passes it
  to sign-in, and `Networking/BackendServices.swift` sends the `deviceId` login parameter
  and saves it in UserDefaults. It is **not** proof of identity or guaranteed permanent across
  reinstalls/vendor-ID changes. Empty/unavailable ID fails eligibility; do not synthesize a fallback.

### Verified active-session lookup boundary (definitions only)

- User's **simple-web-api** corresponds here to `simple-service-webapp-quarkus`:
  **GET `/simple-service-webapp/webapi/myresource/admin`**. Root `/simple-service-webapp`
  and REST subpath `/webapi` are in `src/main/resources/application.properties:4,7`;
  `src/main/java/com/example/rest/ImageResource.java` owns `@Path("/myresource")`,
  `@GET @Path("/admin")` and `getSessions()`.
- That resource forwards incoming **Cookie** to configured `admin.service-url` +
  **GET `/login/activeSessions`**, and passes upstream status/body through; IO failure returns
  502. The lookup source is **dalogin**, not a simple-service database or the `Sessions` DTO.
  `dalogin-quarkus/src/main/java/com/dalogin/servlets/ActiveSessionsServlet.java` reads
  ServletContext **`activeUsers`** and emits a JSON array with **`id`** (enumeration index),
  **`sessionId`** (servlet session ID), **`user`** (session username), **`deviceId`**,
  **`creationTime`**. No `status`, `active`, expiry, or numeric account-ID field exists.
  Missing user/device attributes become empty strings; invalidated sessions caught during
  iteration are skipped. `simple-service-webapp-quarkus/.../api/Sessions.java` has
  `getId/getSessions/getDeviceId`, but this proxy does not serialize that DTO; `sessions`
  is not the actual upstream `sessionId` field.
- `dalogin-quarkus/.../listeners/CustomHttpSessionListener.java` registers sessions at creation
  (before login attributes), evicts older sessions when the same `deviceId` is added, and
  attempts removal/logout cleanup on destruction. `HelloWorld.java:createSession` sets
  `user`/`deviceId` after successful login persistence and sets a 30-minute inactivity interval.
  **User-confirmed (2026-10-04)**: entries returned by this list are active authenticated users,
  so membership is the identity source for WebSocket delivery. Entries with blank `user` or
  `deviceId` (e.g. registered before login attributes) are invalid records, not members.
  creationTime is not an expiry proof; results must be fresh so that logout, expiry, removal or a
  changed mapping stops delivery. The map is ServletContext-local; replica coverage/routing is a
  planning prerequisite.
- **Authorization gap, not a deployed service contract**: `ImageResource.getSessions()` has
  no caller/service authorization check; `ActiveSessionsServlet.doGet()` has none either.
  `dalogin-quarkus/.../filters/AuthFilter.java` maps `/admin/*`, purchases, checkout and logout,
  **not `/activeSessions`**; `src/main/resources/META-INF/web.xml` adds no such security mapping.
  *(User-directed, 2026-10-04)* Authorization of this admin endpoint is **out of scope** for this
  feature. The list is held in memory by dalogin (no DB query for active users). iOS MUST NOT call it.
- Required target resolution: use the authoritative simple-web-api lookup to find the entries
  whose `deviceId` equals the supplied deviceid. Exactly one resolved authenticated `user` (one
  entry, or several entries that agree on the same user) is a match; map that server-returned
  `user` to `login_.logins.id`. No separate WebSocket session credential is required.
  `mbook-quarkus/src/main/java/com/jeet/db/DAO.java:getUser` already queries `Logins` by `user`;
  missing user yields sentinel `id == 0`. No matching entry => no delivery; lookup error, invalid
  record or conflicting users => no delivery with explicit error logging. Reject missing/non-unique
  account resolution; never use the array `id`, device ID or login `uuid` as `logins_id`.

### Accepted WebSocket identity trust model (user-directed, 2026-10-04)

- Fresh membership of the supplied deviceid in the authoritative active-session list establishes
  the **authenticated user associated with that deviceid** under the accepted trust model. It is
  **not** cryptographic proof that the socket sender owns that device.
- Residual risk (accepted, documented): anyone able to present another user's currently active
  deviceId can be mapped to that user and receive that user's screen news while the user is
  subscribed. This design claims no independent spoof protection on the socket. Exposure is
  limited to screen-news payloads (FR-009 contains no personal data); it never authorizes
  preference reads/writes, which stay on the authenticated mbook endpoint (FR-016).
- Delivery still requires the resolved user's `newsScreening` to be exactly `yes`.

## Contract IDs *(mandatory)*

- **CID-MBOOK-WS-SCREEN-NEWS** (new, `planned`): screen-news delivery over the existing `mbook-quarkus` `/mbook-1/ws` endpoint.
- Screen-news subscription read/write (new, `planned`, `CID-MBOOK-NEWS-SETTINGS-SCREEN`): iOS → existing dalogin `AdminServlet`, extended for `GET`/`PUT /login/admin/newsSettings/screen` → mbook `GET`/`PUT /mbook-1/rest/news-settings/screen`, payload `{"enabled":bool}` (plan §3). Existing `/admin` behaviour is unchanged.
- **CID-MBOOKS-SEATS** (referenced only): unchanged. It is listed because `/mbooks-1/ws` is documented as carrying realtime seat updates (see FR-012).

